<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brian O'Rourke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1540–<a href="/years/1591">1591</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Brian na Múrtha Ó Ruairc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Brian O'Rourke was lord of West Breifne in Connacht, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-leitrim">County Leitrim</a>. He resisted English authority, sheltered survivors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a> in 1588 and rose against the governor Richard Bingham. Defeated, he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, where James VI handed him over to the English; he was executed for treason at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyburn">Tyburn</a> in 1591.</p></div>
